Bergamot translator
-------------------

    Files:    dist/electron/translation/engine/, copied at build time from
              the npm package @browsermt/bergamot-translator 0.4.9
    Source:   https://github.com/browsermt/bergamot-translator
    Licence:  Mozilla Public License 2.0
              https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

The engine that translates in reader view, compiled to WebAssembly and run in a
utility process of its own. One file is changed, at build time, by
scripts/build-translation-engine.mjs: in worker/translator-worker.js, two lines
that build file addresses by hand now use Node's fileURLToPath and
pathToFileURL, so the engine finds its own files on Windows, and the two lines
that find its parent use Electron's process.parentPort, since it is not a
worker thread; and WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming is supplied, built from
WebAssembly.instantiate, where that process lacks it. The source of
every original file is at the address above. The language models it runs are not shipped: they are
downloaded from Mozilla when someone first translates a language, under
Mozilla's own terms.


